<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ludwig Wittgenstein</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Wittgenstein</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ludwig Wittgenstein was a philosopher born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> in 1889 into one of the wealthiest families of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a>. He became one of the most influential philosophers of the twentieth century, working mainly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambridge">Cambridge</a>. He is often cited as part of the remarkable intellectual culture of late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> Vienna.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ludwig-wittgenstein.jpg" alt="Ludwig Wittgenstein" width="310" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Moritz Nähr · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ludwig_Wittgenstein_1929.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
